{"id":"2026-07-11-32","date":"2026-07-11","published_at":"2026-07-09T17:55:33Z","observed_at":"2026-07-11T09:27:49+08:00","title":"MulTTiPop: A Multitrack Transcription Dataset for Pop Music","original_url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.08756v1","source_url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.08756v1","source_origin":"primary","source_name":"arXiv Export API","source_type":"paper","source_tier":"Tier 1","source_role":"daily_discovery","review_cadence":"daily","source_mix_note":"arxiv_export_supplement: fresh Atom entry; scanned for paper-candidate or knowledge-gap fit","original_format":"paper","aihot_id":"","aihot_summary":"","aihot_summary_status":"not_applicable","discovery_summary":"We present MulTTiPop, a dataset of pop music segments and their associated multitrack MIDI recordings for the evaluation of automatic music transcription models. MulTTiPop contains 572 segments of popular music totaling 3.5 hours of audio, and contains songs from diverse genres and decades from the 1930s to 2000s. To collect this dataset, we perform metadata-based matching on song segments from the Lakh MIDI and TheoryTab datasets, manually identify an anchor beat between the audio and MIDI, then use beat tracking on the audio and warp the MIDI to match its tempo and timing. We evaluate state-of-the-art automatic music transcription models on MulTTiPop and find substantial room for improvement, with the best model achieving 38% Onset F1. More details and sound examples of MulTTiPop are available at https://gclef-cmu.org/multtipop.","codex_summary":"Fresh arXiv supplement kept for completeness; low direct fit with today AI PM/full-stack focus.","display_summary":"We present MulTTiPop, a dataset of pop music segments and their associated multitrack MIDI recordings for the evaluation of automatic music transcription models. MulTTiPop contains 572 segments of popular music totaling 3.5 hours of audio, and contains songs from diverse genres and decades from the 1930s to 2000s. To collect this dataset, we perform metadata-based matching on song segments from the Lakh MIDI and TheoryTab datasets, manually identify an anchor beat between the audio and MIDI, then use beat tracking on the audio and warp the MIDI to match its tempo and timing. We evaluate state-of-the-art automatic music transcription models on MulTTiPop and find substantial room for improvement, with the best model achieving 38% Onset F1. More details and sound examples of MulTTiPop are available at https://gclef-cmu.org/multtipop.","summary":"We present MulTTiPop, a dataset of pop music segments and their associated multitrack MIDI recordings for the evaluation of automatic music transcription models. MulTTiPop contains 572 segments of popular music totaling 3.5 hours of audio, and contains songs from diverse genres and decades from the 1930s to 2000s. To collect this dataset, we perform metadata-based matching on song segments from the Lakh MIDI and TheoryTab datasets, manually identify an anchor beat between the audio and MIDI, then use beat tracking on the audio and warp the MIDI to match its tempo and timing. We evaluate state-of-the-art automatic music transcription models on MulTTiPop and find substantial room for improvement, with the best model achieving 38% Onset F1. More details and sound examples of MulTTiPop are available at https://gclef-cmu.org/multtipop.","why_it_matters":"Fresh arXiv supplement kept for completeness; low direct fit with today AI PM/full-stack focus.","priority":"P2","confidence":"medium","reading_pack_status":"not_selected","suggested_pool":"archive","candidate_pool":"archive","human_status":"pending","final_pool":"archive","canonical_key":"arxiv.org/abs/2607.08756","duplicate_status":"duplicate_suppressed","duplicate_window_status":"duplicate_in_7d","freshness_status":"fresh_24h","novelty_reason":"7 天内已在 2026-07-10 记录同一链接或同一 canonical_key；本次保留结构化状态，不进入主动阅读包。","practice_fit":"low","reason":"Fresh arXiv supplement kept for completeness; low direct fit with today A